d <ei35 transform> new channels of business . When strategically <ei36 implemented> , an intranet solution will <ei37 provide> the ability to <ei38 mediate> mission-critical , decision support functions in organisations . It will also <ei39 help> further <ei40 improve> communications and collaboration at all levels in an organisation . With intranets in place , it is only logical for organisations to respectively <ei41 link> the network to other companies ' for extended business purposes through extranets . While this will <ei42 enable> the sharing of information among enterprises , security issues such as firewalls and encryption as well as access and control procedures , and the trust levels that enterprises have with each other will <ei43 emerge> and there will be a need to <ei44 address> them . Other than <ei45 usage> in business , Internet technology is also <ei46 beginning> to <ei47 infiltrate> the lifestyle domain . " Smart homes " have <ei48 emerged> <ei49 bringing> a wealth of information and entertainment to families over telecommunications lines . The art of socialising is also <ei50 experiencing> a <ei51 change> where Net / virtual relationships are fast <ei52 overtaking> or <ei53 becoming> parallel with the normal human relationships . Whether this would <ei54 prove> positive or otherwise towards society in the future is yet to be <ei56 seen> . All in all , the Internet <ei57 has> a lot to <ei58 offer> . However , its value and benefits are only as good as how we <ei59 use> it .

