ents <ei35 waiting> then <ei36 begins> to <ei37 increase> , um and , in fact , um over the years many more patients who are about to die of liver tra - uh without a liver transplant would <ei39 accumulate> . If you <ei40 do> the uh alternative extreme , you do n't <ei41 save> as many lives in the early years , by a small fraction . Our system <ei43 is> balanced , it 's right in the middle . And , therefore , it <ei44 works> very well . Nationwide , there are about ten thousand patients <ei45 waiting> for liver transplants each year and only four thousand organs <ei47 become> available for <ei48 transplants> . Secretary Shalala <ei49 says> UNOS five months ago , or <ei51 gave> them five months to <ei53 develop> a new <ei54 plan> to <ei55 distribute> livers which are in the shortest supply . This is VOA Today .

